{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he made the basin of bronze, and its base of bronze, from the mirrors of the serving women.</b> Rashi explained that the basin was made from the mirrors of the women, and there are two reasons why the basin was made from the mirrors of the women. One reason is: because from the basin they would give the suspected adulteresses to drink, therefore the women assisted in the making of the basin, to make known that they were of established fitness and desired the testing of the basin, since they knew of themselves that they were modest. And they gave specifically bronze, because it is stated (Jeremiah 3:3), ״וּמֵצַח אִשָּׁה זוֹנָה הָיָה לָךְ״, and it is written (Isaiah 48:4), ״וּמִצְחֲךָ נְחוּשָׁה״. And it is known that a prosecutor is not made a defender; therefore they gave bronze, for by this they indicated that their forehead was not brazen. The second reason is: that the mirrors are like the water of the basin, which shows face to face; so too the mirrors show face to face. For just as the mirrors tell her whether she is beautiful of form or ugly, so the waters of the basin tell and proclaim whether she strayed or not, and whether she is fit in her deeds." "And it appears that it used the term ״הַצּוֹבְאוֹת״ because the women raised up many hosts in Egypt, and people would say — thinking that the Egyptians had not prevailed over them — for their husbands were afflicted with crushing labor that diminishes propagation and increase, and they certainly became pregnant from the Egyptians. Therefore they wanted to reveal their righteousness: because they had raised up many hosts, they needed to reveal their purity, and they brought those mirrors through which they had raised up those hosts, in order to make the basin from them. As if they said: Look and see and examine us by this — whether we raised those hosts in purity or not, for the basin was made to test suspected adulteresses. And it says: <b>who served at the entrance of the tent of meeting</b> — and still the tent of meeting had not yet been made; therefore they explained that this is the tent of meeting of Moses — see Ibn Ezra and also Rabbeinu Beḥaye. And to me it appears that it speaks entirely of the modesty of the women, as it is written (Genesis 18:9) <b>הִנֵּה בָאֹהֶל</b> — Rashi explained: she is modest. So too those hosts that they raised up — <b>they served at the entrance of the tent</b> — means in their own tent. And the reason it used ״פֶּתַח״ is because it is said of a harlot <b>וַתֵּשֶׁב בְּפֶתַח עֵינַיִם</b> (Genesis 38:14); therefore it says of the modest women <b>פֶּתַח אֹהֶל</b>. And it used <b>מוֹעֵד</b> because there they would meet together with their husbands, who were all day in the fields, for the term מוֹעֵד means those who come from another place to rendezvous in this place."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:41.705501127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}